(5467987, 784654, 24454, '<td valign="top">I had a feeling when I saw this in the challenge that it might be a ribbon contender.  And I think the ever-so-slight blur of the wings adds to the feel of motion making it even more effective than if they had been perfectly tack sharp.  And wow! What a score!  Alot of people get lucky and get personal bests -- but to get a personal best when your highest rated photo is a 7.9+  WOW!  You are becoming legendary :)  And deservingly so, I might add!  Congratulations!!<br/> <br/></td>', 'I had a feeling when I saw this in the challenge that it might be a ribbon contender.  And I think the ever-so-slight blur of the wings adds to the feel of motion making it even more effective than if they had been perfectly tack sharp.  And wow! What a score!  Alot of people get lucky and get personal bests -- but to get a personal best when your highest rated photo is a 7.9+  WOW!  You are becoming legendary :)  And deservingly so, I might add!  Congratulations!! ', '2009-05-04 15:08:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(5467995, 785020, 24454, '<td valign="top">This is really great, Brian!  Mine took a serious nosedive on the last day too!  I even made a comment about that in the scoring thread.  It seems that every single time I have a high scoring photo, it nosedives on the last day -- and I''m noticing alot of other people saying the same thing.  Makes you wonder, doesn''t it!  My guess is your one 2 and your three 3''s were doled out on the last day.  Sorry -- it deserves to be much higher than it finished!<br/> <br/></td>', 'This is really great, Brian!  Mine took a serious nosedive on the last day too!  I even made a comment about that in the scoring thread.  It seems that every single time I have a high scoring photo, it nosedives on the last day -- and I''m noticing alot of other people saying the same thing.  Makes you wonder, doesn''t it!  My guess is your one 2 and your three 3''s were doled out on the last day.  Sorry -- it deserves to be much higher than it finished! ', '2009-05-04 15:13:44.000000', NULL, 0),
